# A display name: not empty, at most 32 bytes of UTF-8, and not the reserved name
law display_name_valid
kind predicate
claim a display name has at least one byte and at most 32 bytes in its UTF-8 form (bytes, not characters)
claim the name "admin" is reserved
source a display-name rule of a sign-up form (the rule is stated here; nothing outside this file defines it)

const max_bytes integer = 32
x-input name text
x-input age integer

require present: len(name) > 0
require short: len(name) <= max_bytes
require free: name != "admin"
require adult: age >= 18

example {"name": "río", "age": 30}

verdict whether the name holds, and the first condition that does not
